From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Seek the DirectShow parser's demuxer to the start
 position on every start.

dmo_parser_init_stream() seeks the demuxer to the current position only
when it is not 0, assuming position 0 means the demuxer is still at the
start of the file. It is not once the filter has streamed: a pause
(preroll, StopWhenReady()) or a previous run makes the demux thread read
ahead, and a stop followed by SetPositions(0) only records the position
while the filter is stopped. The next run then resumes from wherever the
demux thread had read to.

With a raw MPEG-2 video stream (Silent Hill: The Arcade's movies, one
sequence header at the start of each file) the decoder then never gets
the sequence header and decodes nothing: "Invalid frame dimensions 0x0".

Remember that the filter has streamed and seek to position 0 too after
that.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c b/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c
index 10895feb..0a311fd6 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c
@@ -234,6 +234,8 @@ struct dmo_parser
     REFERENCE_TIME stream_start;
 
     HANDLE demux_thread;
+    /* The filter has streamed once: its demuxer has read ahead, it is not at the start. */
+    bool demuxer_moved;
 
     BOOL (*init_streams)(struct dmo_parser *filter, UINT stream_count, INT64 duration);
     BOOL (*check_mime_type)(const WCHAR *mime_type);
@@ -1577,7 +1579,9 @@ static HRESULT dmo_parser_init_stream(struct strmbase_filter *iface)
     /* Seek to the current position (retain seek state across Stop/Pause/Run). */
     {
         LONGLONG seek_time = filter->source_count ? filter->sources[0]->seek.llCurrent : 0;
-        if (seek_time)
+        /* After a previous run (or a pause that prerolled), the demuxer has read ahead:
+         * position 0 needs a seek too. */
+        if (seek_time || filter->demuxer_moved)
         {
             NTSTATUS status;
             WARN("DirectShow parser init seek to %s.\n", debugstr_time(seek_time));
@@ -1590,6 +1594,7 @@ static HRESULT dmo_parser_init_stream(struct strmbase_filter *iface)
     filter->streaming = true;
     filter->flushing = false;
     filter->read_flushing = FALSE;
+    filter->demuxer_moved = true;
 
     for (i = 0; i < filter->source_count; ++i)
     {
